<title>USA: IFR Systems gets $6.4 mln U.S. Army deal.</title>
<headline>IFR Systems gets $6.4 mln U.S. Army deal.</headline>
<dateline>WICHITA, Kan. 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>IFR Systems Inc said it was awarded a $6.4 million contract to supply its AN/GRM-122 test station and related software to the U.S. Army over the next 15 months.</p>
<p>The test station is used for testing and maintenance of specialized wireless communications systems used by the armed forces.</p>
<p>IFR provides electronic test instruments.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
